> I ran through the installer again, and I set the disk up like so:
> 
> /dev/da0a - /
> /dev/da0b - swap

The order in which you assign them is important.  Sysinstall knows that
the swap partition must be `b'.  Also that / must be `a'.  However, if
you first allocate swap and then /, you are telling Sysinstall to put the
`b' partition before the `a' partition on your disk.

